{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YHvALNLACHErKn2ojhdMMi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd037-ln\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/ln: Create Links Between Files\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Build systems, package managers, and configuration tools create hard links and symbolic links\n6\t  to share files without duplication. The macOS BSD ln differs from GNU ln in backup semantics,\n7\t  --no-dereference behavior on symlink targets, and verbose output format. The Go implementation\n8\t  must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gln, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on\n9\t  all flag combinations and edge cases, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Create hard links and symbolic links between files and directories.\n13\t  - G2: Support force-overwrite, interactive, and backup modes for safe link replacement.\n14\t  - G3: Support linking multiple targets into a directory in a single invocation.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Hard link creation (default)\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: Must create a hard link from TARGET to LINK_NAME when invoked as 'ln TARGET LINK_NAME'.\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: Must create hard links for multiple TARGETs in DIRECTORY when invoked as 'ln TARGET... DIRECTORY', placing each link in DIRECTORY with the same basename as the target.\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when attempting to create a hard link to a directory.\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when LINK_NAME already exists and neither -f nor -i is given.\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Symbolic link creation (-s, --symbolic)\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: -s or --symbolic must create a symbolic link instead of a hard link.\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: Must allow symbolic links to directories, unlike hard links.\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: Must store the TARGET string as-is in the symlink, whether it is relative or absolute.\n38\t      - R2.4:\n39\t          text: -r or --relative must create a symbolic link with a relative path from the link location to the target, computing the relative path automatically.\n40\t\n41\t  R3:\n42\t    title: Force, safety, and verbosity flags\n43\t    items:\n44\t      - R3.1:\n45\t          text: -f or --force must remove existing destination files before creating the link.\n46\t      - R3.2:\n47\t          text: -n or --no-dereference must treat a destination that is a symlink to a directory as a regular file, rather than following it.\n48\t      - R3.3:\n49\t          text: |\n50\t            -i or --interactive must prompt the user on stderr before removing an existing\n51\t            destination. Prompt format: 'ln: replace 'DEST'? ' where DEST is the destination\n52\t            path. Read one line from stdin. If the response starts with 'y' or 'Y', proceed\n53\t            with removal and link creation. Any other response (including empty) means decline;\n54\t            do not remove the destination and do not create the link. Do not retry on invalid\n55\t            input. When stdin is not a terminal (detected via os.Stdin.Fd() isatty check),\n56\t            treat as decline (do not prompt, do not remove). When -f and -i are both given,\n57\t            the last flag on the command line wins, matching GNU ln behavior.\n58\t      - R3.4:\n59\t          text: -v or --verbose must print the name of each link created to stdout.\n60\t      - R3.5:\n61\t          text: -b must create a backup of each existing destination file before removal, using the default backup suffix '~'. --backup=METHOD must accept numbered, existing, simple, and none as backup methods.\n62\t      - R3.6:\n63\t          text: -S SUFFIX or --suffix=SUFFIX must use SUFFIX instead of '~' for backup file names.\n64\t\n65\t  R4:\n66\t    title: Differential testing\n67\t    items:\n68\t      - R4.1:\n69\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout, stderr, exit codes, and resulting filesystem state between the Go binary and gln via pkg/testutils.\n70\t      - R4.2:\n71\t          text: \"Tests must cover: hard link creation, symbolic link creation (-s), force overwrite (-f), no-dereference (-n), verbose output (-v), backup creation (-b), multiple targets into a directory, relative symlinks (-r), and error cases for hard linking directories and existing destinations.\"\n72\t      - R4.3:\n73\t          text: Tests must verify that created links point to the correct target and have the correct link type (hard or symbolic), matching gln behavior.\n74\t\n75\tnon_goals:\n76\t  - cmd/ln does not implement -L or -P (logical/physical) dereference modes for following symlink chains on the target.\n77\t  - cmd/ln does not implement -t DIRECTORY or -T (--no-target-directory) flags.\n78\t  - cmd/ln does not read target names from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n79\t\n80\tacceptance_criteria:\n81\t  - id: AC1\n82\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/ln file1 file2 creates a hard link, and both files share the same inode, matching gln.\"\n83\t    traces:\n84\t      - R1.1\n85\t      - R1.2\n86\t      - R1.3\n87\t      - R1.4\n88\t  - id: AC2\n89\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/ln -s target linkname creates a symbolic link pointing to target, matching gln -s.\"\n90\t    traces:\n91\t      - R2.1\n92\t      - R4.2\n93\t  - id: AC3\n94\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/ln -sf newtarget existing_link replaces the existing link, matching gln -sf.\"\n95\t    traces:\n96\t      - R1.1\n97\t      - R1.2\n98\t      - R1.3\n99\t      - R1.4\n100\t  - id: AC4\n101\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/ln -s -r /usr/bin/sort ./sort_link creates a relative symlink, matching gln -s -r.\"\n102\t    traces:\n103\t      - R2.1\n104\t      - R2.4\n105\t      - R4.2\n106\t  - id: AC5\n107\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gln passes for hard links, symlinks, -f, -n, -v, -b, multiple targets, -r, and error cases.\"\n108\t    traces:\n109\t      - R1.3\n110\t      - R1.4\n111\t      - R2.4\n112\t      - R3.1\n113\t      - R3.2\n114\t      - R3.3\n115\t      - R3.4\n116\t      - R3.5\n117\t      - R4.1\n118\t      - R4.2\n119\t  - id: AC6\n120\t    criterion: \"cmd/ln compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n121\t    traces:\n122\t      - R1.1\n123\t      - R1.2\n124\t      - R1.3\n125\t      - R1.4\n126\t      - R2.1\n127\t      - R2.2\n128\t      - R2.3\n129\t      - R2.4\n130\t      - R3.1\n131\t      - R3.2\n132\t      - R3.3\n133\t      - R3.4\n134\t      - R3.5\n135\t      - R3.6\n136\t      - R4.1\n137\t      - R4.2\n138\t      - R4.3\n139\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"acf3b1ba-a30a-4192-8bb7-2343f6098d37","uuid":"92e272b4-103a-495d-a11a-ebca1d38e451","timestamp":"2026-05-19T23:39:52.763Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5318/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd037-ln.yaml","content":"id: srd037-ln\ntitle: \"cmd/ln: Create Links Between Files\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Build systems, package managers, and configuration tools create hard links and symbolic links\n  to share files without duplication. The macOS BSD ln differs from GNU ln in backup semantics,\n  --no-dereference behavior on symlink targets, and verbose output format. The Go implementation\n  must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gln, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on\n  all flag combinations and edge cases, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Create hard links and symbolic links between files and directories.\n  - G2: Support force-overwrite, interactive, and backup modes for safe link replacement.\n  - G3: Support linking multiple targets into a directory in a single invocation.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Hard link creation (default)\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must create a hard link from TARGET to LINK_NAME when invoked as 'ln TARGET LINK_NAME'.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must create hard links for multiple TARGETs in DIRECTORY when invoked as 'ln TARGET... DIRECTORY', placing each link in DIRECTORY with the same basename as the target.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when attempting to create a hard link to a directory.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when LINK_NAME already exists and neither -f nor -i is given.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Symbolic link creation (-s, --symbolic)\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: -s or --symbolic must create a symbolic link instead of a hard link.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must allow symbolic links to directories, unlike hard links.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must store the TARGET string as-is in the symlink, whether it is relative or absolute.\n      - R2.4:\n          text: -r or --relative must create a symbolic link with a relative path from the link location to the target, computing the relative path automatically.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Force, safety, and verbosity flags\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: -f or --force must remove existing destination files before creating the link.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: -n or --no-dereference must treat a destination that is a symlink to a directory as a regular file, rather than following it.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: |\n            -i or --interactive must prompt the user on stderr before removing an existing\n            destination. Prompt format: 'ln: replace 'DEST'? ' where DEST is the destination\n            path. Read one line from stdin. If the response starts with 'y' or 'Y', proceed\n            with removal and link creation. Any other response (including empty) means decline;\n            do not remove the destination and do not create the link. Do not retry on invalid\n            input. When stdin is not a terminal (detected via os.Stdin.Fd() isatty check),\n            treat as decline (do not prompt, do not remove). When -f and -i are both given,\n            the last flag on the command line wins, matching GNU ln behavior.\n      - R3.4:\n          text: -v or --verbose must print the name of each link created to stdout.\n      - R3.5:\n          text: -b must create a backup of each existing destination file before removal, using the default backup suffix '~'. --backup=METHOD must accept numbered, existing, simple, and none as backup methods.\n      - R3.6:\n          text: -S SUFFIX or --suffix=SUFFIX must use SUFFIX instead of '~' for backup file names.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout, stderr, exit codes, and resulting filesystem state between the Go binary and gln via pkg/testutils.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: hard link creation, symbolic link creation (-s), force overwrite (-f), no-dereference (-n), verbose output (-v), backup creation (-b), multiple targets into a directory, relative symlinks (-r), and error cases for hard linking directories and existing destinations.\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: Tests must verify that created links point to the correct target and have the correct link type (hard or symbolic), matching gln behavior.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/ln does not implement -L or -P (logical/physical) dereference modes for following symlink chains on the target.\n  - cmd/ln does not implement -t DIRECTORY or -T (--no-target-directory) flags.\n  - cmd/ln does not read target names from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/ln file1 file2 creates a hard link, and both files share the same inode, matching gln.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/ln -s target linkname creates a symbolic link pointing to target, matching gln -s.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/ln -sf newtarget existing_link replaces the existing link, matching gln -sf.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/ln -s -r /usr/bin/sort ./sort_link creates a relative symlink, matching gln -s -r.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.4\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gln passes for hard links, symlinks, -f, -n, -v, -b, multiple targets, -r, and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R3.5\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/ln compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R3.5\n      - R3.6\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n","numLines":139,"startLine":1,"totalLines":139}}}
